  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In an October 22, 2026 statement, Christopher Pilkerton said proposed regulations were designed to address risks from foreign adversaries benefiting from U.S. investment in key technology sectors and to enhance the Outbound Investment Security Program and national security efforts. In September 2025 Senate testimony and a confirmation response, he emphasized vigilance over how foreign investment enters the country and said he would carefully consider national security risks from technology advances and ensure CFIUS and the Outbound Investment Security Program are responsive. In June 2026, he was reported as framing the issue around potential weaponization and dual-use concerns. In an October 7, 2026 statement, he described the Outbound Investment Security Program as an important tool for addressing the advancement of key technologies by countries of concern that could pose risks to U.S. national security.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s5",
    "s3",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
